WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.850
About two weeks ago Apple refreshed the 5K
iMac with new processors, graphics, ram, and

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.219
I called it the iMac Pro Killer!

00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:09.219
Was I right?

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:13.690
Can this i9 iMac with Vega graphics compete
with a $5000 iMac Pro?

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.480
To give you a Spoiler, yea, and it's actually
faster in some ways.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.630
We’ll be taking a look at Photos and video
editing, gaming performance, connections,

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.630
and more.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.919
Check out the description for links to both
of these machines along with my personal suggestions.

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:28.029
Let's start out with prices.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:32.970
If you spec these Macs as closely as possible
there's only a $750 difference, but the beauty

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.660
of the standard iMac’s is that you have
way more flexibility when ordering so if you

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.380
don’t need a 1TB SSD you’re not forced
to buy one.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:46.980
You can also upgrade RAM yourself which can
save you up to $580, I’ll link to the ram

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.530
we used and our easy install guide down below.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.930
If you’re comparing these two, you likely
need performance but are on a budget so we

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.090
think the configuration purchased makes the
most sense.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.740
You have an 8 core CPU with Vega 48 graphics
and a price savings of around $1600.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.530
On the exterior, the design is practically
the same, other than space gray color of the

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.970
Pro which to be honest looks really nice.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.860
You also get matching peripherals with a full-size
keyboard.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.210
The display are identical which isn’t a
bad thing.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.280
The 5K resolution is still stunning and it's
quite bright with great color accuracy.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.310
At the top, The webcam is better on the iMac
pro being 1080P instead of 720 and along with

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.390
that, the iMac Pro has more better speakers
as well.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:29.409
Moving to the back we no longer have access
to RAM meaning can’t easily upgrade it yourself,

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:33.330
but because of that we have dual fan cooling
which may not make a huge difference with

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:37.330
8 cores but they are definitely needed if
you buy an 18 core model.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.630
One thing that could make you purchase decision
for you is the IO.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.390
The iMac Pro has double the Thunderbolt 3
ports and 10Gbe built in.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:49.820
Not everyone needs these ports, in fact some
won't use them at all but for others two can

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:50.920
be limiting.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:57.170
The only way to add 10Gbe to the standard
iMac is with a thunderbolt adapter, meaning

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.370
you could be left with just one port.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:03.850
Along with that, the SD card slot supports
faster UHS-2 slots.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:10.310
Both CPU’s have 8 cores and 16 threads,
but the clock speed on the i9 is higher, up

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:18.040
to 5Ghz instead of 4.2 which leads us to Geekbench
4’s CPU test where the 2019 iMac has a 25%

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.629
higher single core score.

00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:23.049
This shows how it will perform with simple
single core tasks, so it could actually feel

00:02:23.049 --> 00:02:24.579
more snappy day to day.

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:29.379
Looking at multi-core the i9 imac scores about
8% higher showing off its power when pushing

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:30.379
all cores.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:34.900
In Cinebench R15 which is a rendering benchmark
that pushed the CPU’s to their Max the scores

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.970
are similar but the 2019 iMac still comes
out ahead.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:42.209
These results are impressive to me, seeing
how this iMac with an unchanged single cooling

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:44.310
fan design is beating the iMac Pro.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.230
But what about the graphics, clearly the Vega
56 in the iMac pro is a higher tier card than

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.769
the 48.

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:55.989
In Geekbench 4 the iMac Pro scores 20-25%
higher with Open CL and Metal tests.

00:02:55.989 --> 00:02:59.609
You shouldn’t buy either one of these for
gaming, but say you want to have some fun

00:02:59.609 --> 00:03:01.120
after the work is done.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.249
We tested Unigine heavens extreme preset and
the iMac Pro had only about 5% higher FPS.

00:03:06.249 --> 00:03:10.750
In real-world gaming, that a very small difference
and both of these can perform well with higher

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.779
setting under bootcamp 1440P resolution.

00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:17.310
Check out our dedicated gaming video if you
want to see what performance you can get in

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.310
the real world.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:22.390
Next, let's jump into photo editing, we tested
using Adobe’s Lightroom classic and both

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.370
machines perform very well as they should
you’re editing.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:31.620
Import 50 RAW 42MP image the standard iMac
is slighly faster, Generation 1:1 preview

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.930
the iMac pro is a few seconds faster, and
exporting all edit 50 RAW photos to Jpegs

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.549
took basically the same time.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:41.090
If you edit Photos, there’s practically
no difference.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.760
Now let's jump into video editing.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:50.319
Believe it or not, the standard 5K iMac was
13% faster.

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:55.530
If you edit standard 4K h.264 footage the
i9 iMac is an overall better value especially

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.900
in Premiere, but if you’re starting to work
with H.265 footage the iMac Pro jumps a ways

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.030
ahead because of it T2 Chip which the 2019
iMac doesn’t have.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:07.230
As far as editing smoothness both are fantastic
overall.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:11.339
The graphics cards seem to render stabilization
and effects very similarly in the real world

00:04:11.339 --> 00:04:12.650
which is surprising.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.299
This is a very difficult topic since the results
can vary so much based on your editing program

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:20.419
and even the files you work with so if you
what to know which one is faster for your

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:25.300
use case and why, check out detailed video
editing comparison after this video.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.650
The iMac Pro is a really nice machine, I love
the color, the fact that it has more ports

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:35.210
and updated speakers, Its definitely the nicer
all in one, but its a very expensive machine.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:42.190
Now that Apple went from offering at most
a 4 core i7 to a 5Ghz 8 core i9 and more powerful

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.500
graphics I feel that for most, the standard
iMac provides such a great value.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.470
Unless you need the extra ports, the 2019
i9 iMac provides fantastic performance which

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:56.360
is actually better overall than the iMac pro
at a much lower price.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.930
For most people, its the better choice.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.139
Thank you guys for watching if you want to
see more videos like this one click this circle

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:09.249
above, and check out our detailed gaming and
video editing comparison right over here.

